Subject: Cantor Seeded Compiler Slice 8 Lifecycle Validation MCP SJS Review

@ [review_uuid] f6616a79-c3f6-4844-8a02-507cdf29e943
@ [source_uuid] 526cea59-fda0-47ff-9dac-12ccc7c59d39

& [Delineation]
  + core protocol owns semantic validation
  + MCP adapter owns argument envelope size metadata structured transport and method routing only
  + MCP is_error describes tool-call success versus refusal and cannot replace the typed outcome or verification disposition

& [DataDrivenDesign]
  + [keys] tool_name adapter_profile core_protocol request_id operation
  + [relations] tool_argument contains request adapter delegates_to core response becomes structuredContent
  + [constraints] one tool one request strict top-level object finite bytes direct equivalence stateless stdio fixed annotations

& [DualHemisphereReview]
  + [expansive] later custody handles may shrink the full request and a host may install this server for Codex or llama.cpp tool calls
  + [convergent] P0 carries the full request in one stateless call and adds no registry handle state resource prompt or transport variant

& [SevenFoldExplosion]
  + [identity] distinct adapter server tool request and response identities
  + [schema] closed top-level argument with strict nested runtime deserialization
  + [bounds] wrapper byte ceiling accounts JSON overhead above the core eight-megabyte request ceiling
  + [delegation] one direct call to the closed core function
  + [honesty] short text points to structuredContent and repeats no ungrounded success claim
  + [security] no state secret key runner network write or ambient discovery
  + [growth] later custody or host configuration requires separate authority

& [PruningTrace]
  + pruned extension of existing cantor-mcp because it would alter published tool discovery and resident-mode behavior
  + pruned full generated nested JSON Schema because it would enlarge model-visible metadata while runtime strictness already belongs to core forms
  + pruned JSON string arguments because a request object remains more natural to tool callers

& [Exhaustion]
  + [state] phase_locked_for_one_stateless_read_only_stdio_tool
  + [next] separately govern custody compression or host installation after adapter proof
